      {
        "date": "2026-11-09",
        "id": "paper:721d75f62f63498e",
        "kind": "paper",
        "label": "Nov 9, 2026 10:56 AM CT",
        "note": "6, 2026, Purpose Entertainment hosted the Artemis Celebration Gala at NASA’s Kennedy Space Center Visitor Complex in Merritt Island, Florida. Held on the eve of NASA’s MAX POWER event, the gala celebrated the explorers, innovators, and visionaries advancing the next era of human spaceflight.",
        "published": "2026-11-09T10:56:29-06:00",
        "section": "Frontier lab",
        "severity": "",
        "source": "NASA",
        "title": "Astronauts Across Generations Share the Stage",
        "url": "https://www.nasa.gov/image-article/astronauts-across-generations-share-the-stage/"
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-11-09",
        "id": "paper:48684d18833a74ee",
        "kind": "paper",
        "label": "Nov 9, 2026 10:07 AM CT",
        "note": "Thousands gathered over several days in early November to experience MAX POWER – NASA’s first exhibition of America’s superiority in space, aeronautics, and technology on and around the agency’s Kennedy Space Center in Florida. The multi-day, family-friendly event honored the nation’s 250th anniversary and served as a culmination of the agency’s Inspiration Tour.",
        "published": "2026-11-09T10:07:10-06:00",
        "section": "Frontier lab",
        "severity": "",
        "source": "NASA",
        "title": "MAX POWER: NASA’s Inaugural Aerospace Expo Ignites America’s Future",
        "url": "https://www.nasa.gov/general/max-power-nasas-inaugural-aerospace-expo-ignites-americas-future/"
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-11-09",
        "id": "paper:b1a39ceff126228a",
        "kind": "paper",
        "label": "Nov 9, 2026 10:01 AM CT",
        "note": "NASA’s two ESCAPADE (Escape and Plasma Acceleration and Dynamics Explorers) spacecraft have each successfully completed a powered Earth flyby, using Earth’s gravity in combination with a sustained engine burn to slingshot themselves toward Mars. With these successful maneuvers complete, the twin spacecraft are on target to reach the Red Planet in September 2027.",
        "published": "2026-11-09T10:01:47-06:00",
        "section": "Frontier lab",
        "severity": "",
        "source": "NASA",
        "title": "NASA’s ESCAPADE Completes Powered Earth Flybys, Now En Route to Mars",
        "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/science-research/heliophysics/nasas-escapade-completes-powered-earth-flybys-now-en-route-to-mars/"
      },
      {
        "date": "2026-11-09",
        "id": "paper:71ad6e560653f98a",
        "kind": "paper",
        "label": "Nov 9, 2026 9:40 AM CT",
        "note": "Scientists from Tokyo Metropolitan University have discovered that charged states made of two electrons and a positively charged hole (or vice versa) on atomically thin rolls of carbon atoms have a structure-derived \"handedness\" in how they interact with light. While electron-hole pairs, or \"excitons,\" were known to keep the chirality of the underlying nanotube, the team showed that adding a charge to create \"trions\" does not change this property.",
        "published": "2026-11-09T09:40:01-06:00",
        "section": "Frontier lab",
        "severity": "",
        "source": "Phys.org physics",
        "title": "Chirality of 'trions' illuminates new paths for quantum optics",
        "url": "https://phys.org/news/2026-11-chirality-trions-illuminates-paths-quantum.html"
      },
